From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 11:44:47 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: aop_audio: Defer probing until the AOP has
 published

The probe borrows the AOP core's driver data from its parent device as
a pinned box. The core registers its service devices from a workqueue
while it is still probing, and the driver core publishes a driver's
data only once that probe returns, so a microphone device that probes
early borrows a null pointer as an Arc.

68c305f20c08 ("iio: common: aop_sensors: Defer probing until the AOP
has published") added AOP::from_child() for exactly this and moved the
sensor drivers to it, and the T8140 audio driver uses it too, but this
driver still open-codes the lookup. Use from_child(), which returns
EPROBE_DEFER until the core has bound, check that the service record
the core attaches as platform data is present, and fail the probe
instead of panicking when the device has no parent.

Fixes: 3f89f537dacb ("ASoC: apple: Add aop_audio driver")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 sound/soc/apple/aop_audio.rs | 19 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/aop_audio.rs b/sound/soc/apple/aop_audio.rs
index 04b756c2ef..3e2835bf64 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/aop_audio.rs
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/aop_audio.rs
@@ -976,12 +976,19 @@ impl platform::Driver for SndSocAopDriver {
     ) -> impl PinInit<Self::Data<'bound>, Error> + 'bound {
         let info = info.ok_or(ENODEV)?;
         let dev = ARef::<device::Device>::from(pdev.as_ref());
-        let parent = pdev.as_ref().parent().unwrap();
-        // SAFETY: our parent is AOP, and AopDriver is repr(transparent) for Arc<dyn Aop>
-        let adata_ptr = unsafe { Pin::<KBox<Arc<dyn AOP>>>::borrow(parent.get_drvdata()) };
-        let adata = (&*adata_ptr).clone();
-        // SAFETY: AOP sets the platform data correctly
-        let svc = unsafe { *((*dev.as_raw()).platform_data as *const EPICService) };
+        let parent = pdev.as_ref().parent().ok_or(ENODEV)?;
+        // SAFETY: this is a service device the AOP core registered, being
+        // probed here; the lookup defers the probe until the core has
+        // published its driver data.
+        let adata = unsafe { <dyn AOP>::from_child(pdev.as_ref()) }?;
+        // SAFETY: the AOP core sets this child's platform data to the EPIC
+        // service it created the child for; it lives as long as the child.
+        let service = unsafe { (*dev.as_raw()).platform_data as *const EPICService };
+        if service.is_null() {
+            return Err(ENODEV);
+        }
+        // SAFETY: the pointer was checked above and stays valid with the child.
+        let svc = unsafe { *service };
         let parent_fwnode = parent.fwnode().ok_or(ENOENT)?;
         let fwnode = parent_fwnode
             .get_child_by_name(c_str!("audio"))
